.TH PLASMA 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
plasma \- run a PLASMA module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plasma
.I module
.RI [ arg ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Load the maux PLASMA runtime and execute a module with its arguments.
The runtime is /mnt/MAUX/PLRT (the seed opens that exact name); support modules
are installed under /mnt/MAUX/PLLIB.
The module and its dependencies must have been built for this port.
.PP
The seed provides the PLASMA virtual machine and the maux system-call
bridge. It does not by itself compile source.
Cooked programs, including the production NAS, bind their runtime and
module closure into an executable and are invoked by their own name.
They do not require an explicit plasma prefix.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/PLASMA  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
nas(1), plasm(1), proshim(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The module supplies its normal exit status. Seed usage errors return 2; runtime loading failures return 1.
.SH BUGS
Only the maux runtime ABI and installed modules are supported, not arbitrary Apple II PLASMA applications. The interpreter/compiler development images supply this command; it is not on the ordinary play roster.
